======

If they all have to be the same weight, then the sum of all numbers / 3 is the
way to go. Therefore we want to find which number that adds to that numbers, 
is the lowest in terms of QE. 

Now, we need to loop every combination of every number with every other ones,
and we should start at the highest number. So we should sort. I will just do a
simple bubblesort... Our inputs are sorted, so we just begin at the end

yeah no, this dont work. We need combinatorics, and treat this as a tree. Recurse
through the tree, the bottom will have each path, and therefore each unique 
combination. We store that, go left and right, left means pass nothing, right we
pass along each levels number.
